the netflix fantasy series curse makes a  lot of changes to the classic arthurian  legend  and raises a lot of new mysteries here  are some of the biggest questions which  are still left unanswered by the end of  the show's first season  from the very beginning curse lets us  know that nimwei is eventually doomed to  sink into a deep body of water  while bleeding from multiple arrow  wounds during the closing minutes of the  first season  we finally see how that happens while  attempting to save a wounded merlin  alongside morgana  nimwei is confronted by a bow and  arrow-wielding sister iris  iris ignores limway's pleas for mercy  and fires several arrows into her  despite merlin's attempt to save her  nimway tumbles from the bridge  disappearing into the churning waters  below and leaving the sword of power  abandoned on the bridge  when last we see her nimwei is sinking  to her supposed death  recalling the image that opened the  season however despite all signs  pointing to nimway dying  her role in the arthurian legend as the  mystical lady of the lake  indicates that she'll survive somehow  nimway showed herself capable of  tremendous magic throughout the course  of the season  maybe merlin will use his magic to save  her or perhaps nimwei will save herself  through her own magic  when nimwei realizes that merlin is her  biological father  she finally understands why her mother  tasked her with bringing the sword of  power to him  even more pieces fall into place when  merlin shows her the circumstances that  led to her own conception  the two met when nimway's mother lenore  healed merlin from something inside his  chest that was causing him pain  she promptly cut him open to extract it  and was shocked to pull out the very  sword of power  that nimwei returns to him years later  merlin mentions that the sword was his  once but never explains how it ended up  inside him  the most he offers is that it wasn't an  enemy who did it but beyond that  we never get any information on what the  sword was doing inside merlin's body was  he hiding it was it a curse  we may never know or at least not by the  end of season one  merlin insinuates several times and he's  actually hundreds of years old  but we never uncover the reason behind  his staggeringly long life  originally merlin was born into the  faith but his powers seem to exceed  those of the other fae that we meet  when we encounter merlin and curse he's  been without his magic for some time  and we later learn that he's lost his  powers when lenore extracted the sword  of power from his body  merlin spends most of the season  endeavoring to get his magic back  through various methods  and as he does he winds up brushing  against death quite a few times  at one point after having been stabbed  multiple times through the chest  he even asked a rhetorical question why  can't i die  it's a good question not only should his  stab wounds have been mortal but he was  shot in the heart with an arrow earlier  in the same episode  we see plenty of other fade die over the  course of cursed so what makes merlin  different  probably one of the biggest twists curse  throws at his audience comes when we  learn the true identity of the weeping  monk that has been terrorizing the fae  for the entire season  a long time ago my name was lancelot the  weeping monk's adopted father is father  karden  leader of the red paladins who despised  the fae and their magic  but midway through the series gawain the  green knight recognizes the weeping monk  as a fellow faye  by the end of the season the weeping  monk has turned on his adoptive father  saving the young feyboy squirrel yet the  reveal that the monk was actually named  lancelot before he was taken by father  cardian  still comes as quite a shock cardin  tells lancelot that he spared him from  the slaughter of his village  because of his ability to sense other  fae but considering karden's track  record  we can't believe that that's a complete  story we're curious to learn more about  the young lancelot before kardin took  him  while curse is upfront about the  identities of legendary characters such  as merlin and arthur  it enjoys doling out the more famous  names of other characters throughout the  course of the season  on several occasions characters we've  met under one name reveal that their  actual name is much more familiar  it grains my grandmother's name it's a  bit of a mix up when they first brought  me here  to friends i'm morgana go squirrel  i won't leave you here it begs a  question of whether there are any other  well-known arthurian characters who have  already made an appearance but under  different names  since curse plays pretty fast and loose  for the characters backstories we can't  rule anyone out  after all if the chivalrous knight  lancelot can be introduced as one of the  season's most terrifying villains  anything is possible perhaps sister iris  or pym will eventually turn out to be  familiar characters  from the legend or a minor character  will turn out to be more mythologically  important than we thought  something about virus has always seemed  a little strange starting with her first  meeting with nimway where iris reveals  how she can spot demons  i just stare at them i stare at them  until i see through their faces to their  real faces  it's clear that iris and nimway are  likely not going to be friends  and sure enough iris is soon burning  down the abbey and attempting to find  the red paladins determined to join  their bloody cause by killing nimway  but while iris is certainly motivated by  a strong hatred of the fae and their  magic  there seems to be more to her than that  several times she seems to be internally  conflicted  about the path she's set for herself and  at one point she punishes herself for  straying from her task  by burning her own arm over an open  flame berating herself  as though she's of two minds between her  radical hatred her unflinching capacity  for violence  and her strange internal debates we  wonder if there's a lot more to sister  iris than meets eye  when nimway asks merlin about the sword  of power he admits that it was once his  and that at one time he might have  desired it again however he claims his  motives have since changed  let me destroy it what  that's my true intention if you must  know it it turns out merlin did want the  sword back almost immediately after  lenoir extracted it from his chest  since he realized the sword was tied to  his magic at the time lenore lied and  told him that she had destroyed the  sword but by the time he learns that  nimwei is his daughter  he seems to have experienced a true  change of heart and seems sincere about  destroying the sword  yet by the end of the season merlin's  magic has returned and it seems to be  tied directly to his reclaiming of the  sword the last we see of him he survives  only by channeling the sword's magic  will he still be committed to destroying  the sword now that he's had a taste of  its power again  we'll have to find out nimwei may be the  character who spends the most time with  the sword of power but merlin has the  longest history with the magical object  the first indication of merlin's  connection to the sword came when he was  struck by lightning  and branded with a sword-shaped burn  mark that ran the length of his body  later we learned that the sword was at  one time merlin's that has somehow wound  up embedded inside his body  and that his magic has somehow linked to  it yet for every small detail we do know  there's plenty we don't  where did the sword come from before it  came into merlin's possession and how  did it get so strongly linked to him  what is the source and extent of its  magical abilities for an object that was  at the center of most of the conflicts  in cursed first season  we actually know very little about it  and are eager to learn more  midway through kurt's first season king  uther pendragon receives a rude  awakening when he learns that he is not  in fact  royal by birth and it always assumed it  turns out that when his mother was  pregnant with her son  complications in childbirth led to the  baby being delivered still born  the king had just died several months  prior and desperate for an heir the  queen sent her midwife out to pay a  local peasant to give up her baby  the midwife returned the baby to the  queen who raised him as her own  utha learns that his biological mother  was named sylvia  and that she died shortly after giving  up her child at the age of only 19.  enraged uther poisons the queen with  spiced wine which is the same method she  used to kill sylvia however as far as we  know  sylvia was the only member of his family  ever killed as part of the queen's  cover-up which means his father may  still be out there somewhere along with  other members of his family will he go  seeking them or will he eventually track  him down  we'll have to wait and see once the  truth of uther's illegitimacy begins to  come to light  the viking ruler come by the ice king  arrives with a claim to the throne  although cumber claims to have pain  dragon lineage it is never clarified  exactly what his relationship to the  late king was the most we learn is when  the midwife gives cumber a blood-soaked  cloth  presumably from the queen's stillbirth  this is the blood of my cousin  it is my lord perhaps his use of the  word cousin means that cumber was the  king's nephew however  cousin could also be a broader term  referring to any distant relative  in which case cumber's bloodline could  have diverged with the pen dragons  several generations earlier it will be  interesting to see whether the  connection between cumber and the pen  dragons  is explored further in future seasons  and exactly what that connection is  many times throughout curse uther seems  to refer to himself in the plural  using pronouns like we and our to  express his thoughts and opinions  tear us down and you will suffer  as we suffer there doesn't appear to be  much rhyme or reason to when he uses  plural pronouns and when he refers to  himself  as i begging the question of what  exactly is going on here  maybe uther is referring to either his  kingdom or his court when he speaks in  the plural  but that doesn't feel like what is  happening at times it almost seems like  there may be multiple consciousnesses  warring inside him  yet no one ever seems to blink at his  fluid oscillation between singular and  plural pronouns  suggesting that either no one notices or  everyone has just accepted it as a  strange quirk  we have to wonder who uther is referring  to whenever he says we  and if we'll ever learn any more about  them the mysterious shrouded character  known only as the widow  appears in a handful of episodes to warn  characters that death may be swiftly  approaching  while it's obvious that the widow has  one foot in the world of the living and  the other in the world of the dead  very little has ever communicated about  her identity some sort of shared history  with merlin is hinted at but no real  detail is ever given  adding another intriguing layer to the  mystery of the widow is that she's not  actually immortal  morgana actually manages to kill her  off-screen toward the end of season 1  and subsequently takes her place even  more ghana herself isn't entirely sure  how it happens  but her becoming the new widow suggests  that the previous widow was also one  someone else entirely  was she someone merlin new how did she  become the widow  and who was the widow before her we'll  just have to hold out hope that curse  gets a second season so we can find out  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

